cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it. The author list is a placeholder
  and is being settled; see the comment at the top of this file.
title: "g16dump: FCIDUMP files for SHCI and DMRG from Gaussian 16 windowed MO integrals"
abstract: >-
  Builds FCIDUMP files for selected-CI (Dice) and DMRG (Block2) solvers from a
  Gaussian 16 matrix-element file, without ever transforming integrals over the
  full MO space. Gaussian transforms the two-electron integrals over the active
  window only; the frozen core is folded analytically into an effective
  one-electron Hamiltonian and a scalar core energy. The open-shell algebra is
  exact for ROHF references whose alpha and beta Fock matrices are available,
  and the alpha/beta agreement is checked rather than assumed.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lgutsev/FCIDUMP_Exporter"
keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - FCIDUMP
  - Gaussian 16
  - selected configuration interaction
  - DMRG
  - active space
  - frozen core

